soc: sunxi: h713-mips: cycle the panel's supply after a restart (HY300PRO-G-EU)

On the HY300PRO-G-EU (HY200 QZ713DF A1, a 1280x720 LCD panel with its own
timing controller) every restart of the display firmware left the wall
black with the lamp on: the firmware came up ready, the HDMI picture was
detected, and every register of the display chain read as after a good
boot - the panel had lost the LVDS clock while the firmware restarted and
did not lock again. The HY310's DLP bridge locks again by itself.

Measured 09./10.10.2026 on that board: the panel's reset pulse alone (PH16
low 2 ms) did not bring the picture back; its supply off for 300 ms and on
again (PF6, the stock panel_power_en U-Boot drives at boot) did, with and
without the reset, three of three by hand. So the driver takes two
optional properties, panel-power-gpios and panel-reset-gpios, requested as
U-Boot left them, and after every start that ends ready cycles the supply
as U-Boot powers the panel: off 300 ms, on, 20 ms, reset 2 ms. The board's
tree names PF6 and PH16; a board without them is not touched. With it,
three restarts through h713-mips-restart in a row brought the picture
back each time, 3.2 s after the start.

PF6 needs to be in the pin controller's table for the request (separate
patch); without it the probe defers for good.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
